-- title:
--   Splitting bound for a graded piece of a quotient by a product
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, $G$ an additive abelian group, $w:\sigma\to G$ a weight function and $R=K[x_\sigma]$. For $d\in G$ let $R_d\subseteq R$ be the $K$-subspace of polynomials that are weighted homogeneous of weight $d$ (every monomial $x^m$ occurring has $\sum_sm_sw(s)=d$), and for $p\in R$ let $[p]_d$ be its weight-$d$ component. For an ideal $J\subseteq R$ write
--   $$Q_d(J)=R_d\big/(J\cap R_d)$$
--   for the weight-$d$ piece of the quotient by $J$. Call $J$ *component-closed* if $[p]_d\in J$ for all $p\in J$ and all $d\in G$; these are exactly the weighted homogeneous ideals.
--
--   Let $I$ be a component-closed ideal, let $a\in R$ be weighted homogeneous of weight $e\in G$, let $b\in R$ be arbitrary, and let $d\in G$ be such that $R_d$ and $R_{d-e}$ are finite-dimensional. Then
--   $$\dim_K Q_d\bigl(I+(ab)\bigr)\ \le\ \dim_K Q_d\bigl(I+(a)\bigr)+\dim_K Q_{d-e}\bigl(I+(b)\bigr).$$
--
--   This is the inductive step for bounding the Hilbert function of an ideal generated by products: adding the product $ab$ to $I$ leaves a piece no larger than what remains after adding $a$, plus what remains after adding $b$ in the degree shifted by the weight of $a$. Iterating it over a list of products leads to a sum over all ways of choosing one factor from each product.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $Q_d(J)$ is `componentQuotient w J d`, the quotient of `weightedHomogeneousSubmodule K w d` by the preimage of $J$ under the inclusion, and dimensions are `Module.finrank K`. Component-closedness is `ComponentClosed w I`. Finite-dimensionality of $R_d$ and $R_{d-e}$ enters as `Module.Finite` instances.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Algebra/Determinantal/Multigraded.lean#L100-L153

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_SmoothInitialForm
import Definitions.Def_OAI_Algebra_Determinantal_Multigraded

open OAI OAI.PermanentBorder OAI.PermanentBorder.Multigraded
open MvPolynomial
variable {K σ G : Type*} [Field K] [AddCommGroup G]
variable (w : σ → G)

theorem OAI.PermanentBorder.Multigraded.finrank_product_split (I : Ideal (MvPolynomial σ K))
    (hI : ComponentClosed w I) {a b : MvPolynomial σ K} {e : G}
    (ha : a.IsWeightedHomogeneous w e) (d : G)
    [Module.Finite K (Piece (K := K) w d)]
    [Module.Finite K (Piece (K := K) w (d-e))] :
    Module.finrank K (componentQuotient w (I ⊔ Ideal.span {a*b}) d) ≤
      Module.finrank K (componentQuotient w (I ⊔ Ideal.span {a}) d) +
      Module.finrank K (componentQuotient w (I ⊔ Ideal.span {b}) (d-e)) := by sorry
